# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# Without this file Vercel falls back to .gitignore, which excludes ALL of
# public/data/*.json -- including the bounded index the deployment needs. The
# result builds cleanly and then 503s on every search, which is the worst
# possible failure: it looks like a working deploy.

node_modules
.next
.git
.vercel

# The full corpus. 382MB and 775MB respectively -- far past any serverless
# bundle limit, and the reason jobs-deploy.json exists.
public/data/jobs-v2.json
public/data/jobs-v2-full.json
public/data/jobs-snapshot.json
public/data/ibm-jobs.json

# Crawler state: large, machine-local, and meaningless in a read-only runtime.
.ingest-state.json

# Backups the pipeline writes beside the index it is about to rewrite.
#
# These are ignored by git (*.bak) but .gitignore is NOT consulted when this
# file exists, so they were being uploaded: 118MB of them, as
# public/data/jobs-deploy.json.pre-earlycareer.bak and its shard. Everything
# under public/ is publicly servable, so a superseded copy of the whole index
# was downloadable at its own URL -- stale job data served as though current,
# to anyone who guessed the name.
*.bak
public/data/*.bak

# The vendored location dataset is ~2.5GB of SQL/CSV used only by seed scripts.
countries-states-cities-database

# Offline research exports.
docs/reports

*.log

# Crawl corpora. NOTE: when .vercelignore exists, .gitignore is NOT consulted,
# so anything ignored only by git still gets uploaded. data/workday alone is
# 667MB (a 483MB ndjson and a 214MB links file), which trips Vercel's 100MB
# per-file limit and fails the deploy outright -- the error names the limit but
# not the file.
#
# Nothing under data/ is read at runtime: the one match for "data/" in app/ and
# lib/ is part of a remote USCIS URL in lib/visa/sponsor-registers.ts, not a
# local path. These are inputs to scripts, not to the running site.
data/workday
data/financial
walmart-roles.json
walmart-roles.ndjson

# Named individuals (see .gitignore). Not withheld from a public git repo only
# to be uploaded to a public deployment instead.
data/recruiter-evidence
